```python
class Solution:
    def minOperations(self, nums: list[int]) -> int:
        n = len(nums)
        ans = -1
        # Case A: rotation of sorted
        k = nums[0]
        if all(nums[i] == (k + i) % n for i in range(n)):
            ans = min(n - k, k + 2)
        # Case B: rotation of reversed sorted
        k = n - 1 - nums[0]
        if all(nums[i] == n - 1 - ((k + i) % n) for i in range(n)):
            cost = min(k, n - k) + 1
            ans = cost if ans == -1 else min(ans, cost)
        return ans
```

Note: the `all` with generator is O(n) each, fine. But early termination helps. Could also use a loop. n up to 1e5, two passes fine.

